    "created_at": "2017-04-17T14:06:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-17T14:06:45Z",
    "body": "For `[[DefineOwnProperty]]`,\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#windowproxy-defineownproperty\r\n> If P is an array index property name, return false.\r\n\r\nI think that it is expected that author script can never define a property with an array index property name.  Even when `window.length < n`, we don't want to allow author script to actually set `window[n] = 42`, which may be shadowed when a new iframe is added.  Allowing it is quite confusing.\r\nSo, I'm happy with this part as is.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor `[[GetOwnProperty]]`,\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#windowproxy-getownproperty\r\n> Return PropertyDescriptor{ [[Value]]: value, [[Writable]]: false, [[Enumerable]]: false, [[Configurable]]: true }.\r\n\r\nProbably, this statement should be replaced with something like:\r\n> If value is undefined, then return undefined, otherwise return PropertyDescriptor{...}.\r\n\r\nBoth of Firefox and Chrome are doing:\r\n`Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window, window.length) => undefined`\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
