    "created_at": "2017-04-17T16:22:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-17T16:22:25Z",
    "body": "For `[[GetOwnProperty]]`, Safari also returns `undefined`.\r\n`Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window, window.length) => undefined`\r\n\r\nFor `[[DefineOwnProperty]]`, Safari's behavior is the same as Chrome.  We can actually set `window[0] = 42`, and then `window[0]` evaluates to `42`.  Chrome will soon change the behavior, though, as I landed https://crrev.com/2816743002 .\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
